va_gpt2_k3 and mvp_sva_gpt2_k3_topk. The median tier prediction shows SVA achieving css_1.00 with a CPR improvement between 0.005 and 0.03, technically passing condition④ but without strong statistical backing. Looking at the actual data, the SVA css_1.00 version gives a mean CPR of 1.1738 versus the best single model at 1.1676, yielding a delta of 0.0062. The topk variant shows 1.1873 versus 1.1703, giving 0.017. So the median prediction needs to align with this observed range.\n\nGPT-2 on factual and document QA tasks is likely abandoned since the model lacks sufficient capacity for reliable factual recall. For Qwen-2.5 0.5B on IOI with K=3, I'm now using ACDC top-k instead of IFR, though the results are mixed with Jaccard scores between 0.3 and 0.55, and CSS results showing one pass, one fail, or mostly marginal outcomes. The arithmetic variant also switches to ACDC top-k but is expected to underperform given the high Jaccard difficulty. Gemma-2 2B on IOI hasn't been attempted yet, and Llama-3 is the next in the queue.\n\nI've completed the binarization sensitivity sweep with partial stability, partially worked through ablation method comparisons, finished the CIRCUS negative ablation, and analyzed the Jaccard-CSS correlation with a few data points showing a visible trend but not statistically significant. Now I'm writing out the full YAML configuration, making sure the numbers align precisely with the defined ranges.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14866,"cache_read_input_tokens":43568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14866},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fa4408e-fc3a-466c-8bb9-049ddeee63fb","uuid":"e74c755c-127c-48a6-93ee-0f4c26a5314e"}
